{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-333311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+1){y}^{2}-3y+x$\n- ${y}^{′}=x{y}^{3}+2y-1$\n- $y{y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Riccati differential equation with \n\n$$\na(x)={x}^{2}+1,\\,b(x)=-3,\\,c(x)=x.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{3}+2y-1\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a ${y}^{3}$ term.\n\n- Equation III is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+\\frac{5}{y}.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation because it contains a $\\frac{5}{y}$ term instead of a combination involving only ${y}^{2}$, $y$, and a function of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=(x-1){y}^{2}+2xy+{x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{3}-y+{e}^{x}$\n- $y{y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+1){y}^{2}-3$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x)=x-1,\\,b(x)=2x,\\,c(x)={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{3}-y+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a ${y}^{3}$ term.\n\n- Equation III is not a Riccati differential equation.Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+1)y-\\frac{3}{y}.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation because it contains a $\\frac{3}{y}$ term instead of a combination involving only ${y}^{2}$, $y$, and a function of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=2{y}^{3}-xy+1$\n- ${y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+3){y}^{2}-4y+{e}^{x}$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{y}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{y}^{3}-xy+1.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a ${y}^{3}$ term.\n\n- Equation II is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x)={x}^{2}+3,\\,b(x)=-4,\\,c(x)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{y}.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation because it contains a $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{y}$ term instead of a combination involving only ${y}^{2}$, $y$, and a function of $x$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={y}^{3}-2xy+5$\n- $y{y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4$\n- ${y}^{′}-4y=(x-2){y}^{2}+{e}^{x}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{3}-2xy+5.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a ${y}^{3}$ term.\n\n- Equation II is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+\\frac{4}{y}.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation because it contains a $\\frac{4}{y}$ term instead of a combination involving only ${y}^{2}$, $y$, and a function of $x.$\n\n- Equation III is a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(x-2){y}^{2}+{e}^{x}+4y.\n$$\n\nThis is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x)=x-2,\\,b(x)=4,\\,c(x)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={y}^{3}-2xy+4$\n- ${y}^{′}=6x{y}^{2}+3y-x$\n- ${y}^{′}+5y=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+7$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{3}-2xy+4.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a ${y}^{3}$ term.\n\n- Equation II is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x)=6x,\\,b(x)=3,\\,c(x)=-x.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+7-5y.\n$$\n\nThis is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x)=2{x}^{2},\\,b(x)=-5,\\,c(x)=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(x+1){y}^{2}-xy-1.\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=1.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=0$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+1\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}=(x+1)(z+1)^{2}-x(z+1)-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′} & =(x+1)({z}^{2}+2z+1)-xz-x-1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =(x+1){z}^{2}+(x+2)z \\\\ {z}^{′}-(x+2)z & =(x+1){z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=-(x+2),\\,Q(x)=x+1,\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333781" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{-x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{-x}{y}^{2}-(x+2{e}^{-2x})y+(x{e}^{-x}-{e}^{-x}+{e}^{-3x}).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{-x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-{e}^{-x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{-x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-{e}^{-x}={e}^{-x}(z+{e}^{-x})^{2}-(x+2{e}^{-2x})(z+{e}^{-x})+(x{e}^{-x}-{e}^{-x}+{e}^{-3x}).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-{e}^{-x} & ={e}^{-x}(z+{e}^{-x})^{2}-(x+2{e}^{-2x})(z+{e}^{-x})+(x{e}^{-x}-{e}^{-x}+{e}^{-3x}) \\\\ {z}^{′}-{e}^{-x} & ={e}^{-x}{z}^{2}-xz-{e}^{-x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+xz & ={e}^{-x}{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=x,\\,Q(x)={e}^{-x},\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333790" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-3y+2.\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=1.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=0$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+1\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}=(z+1)^{2}-3(z+1)+2.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′} & =(z+1)^{2}-3(z+1)+2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={z}^{2}-z \\\\ {z}^{′}+z & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=1,\\,Q(x)=1,\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333607" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{y}^{2}-(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4)y+(4{sin}^{2}⁡x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=4(z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}-(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4)(z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+(4{sin}^{2}⁡x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =4(z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}-(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4)(z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+(4{sin}^{2}⁡x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ {z}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =4{z}^{2}-4z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {z}^{′}+4z & =4{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=4,\\,Q(x)=4,\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333792" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/ref