lution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4x\\,{y}^{2}-(16x+3)y+(16x+6).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=2.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=0$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+2\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}=4x(z+2)^{2}-(16x+3)(z+2)+(16x+6).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′} & =4x(z+2)^{2}-(16x+3)(z+2)+(16x+6) \\\\ {z}^{′} & =4x{z}^{2}-3z \\\\ {z}^{′}+3z & =4x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=3,\\,Q(x)=4x,\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333902" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}{y}^{2}-2{e}^{2x}y+{e}^{3x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}{y}^{2}-2{e}^{2x}y+{e}^{3x}+{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)={e}^{x},\\,b(x)=-2{e}^{2x},\\,c(x)={e}^{3x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+{e}^{x}={e}^{x}(z+{e}^{x})^{2}-2{e}^{2x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{3x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}({z}^{2}+2{e}^{x}z+{e}^{2x})-2{e}^{2x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{3x}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}{z}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={e}^{x}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-{e}^{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C} \\\\ y-{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}+{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}-C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{x}+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-\\frac{4}{x}y+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-\\frac{4}{x}y+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=1,\\,b(x)=-\\frac{4}{x},\\,c(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+\\frac{2}{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=(z+\\frac{2}{x})^{2}-\\frac{4}{x}(z+\\frac{2}{x})+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & =({z}^{2}+\\frac{4z}{x}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})-(\\frac{4z}{x}+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {z}^{′}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & ={z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-\\frac{2}{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y-\\frac{2}{x} & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-333805" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333805" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{1}{x+C}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2}{x+C}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2}{x-C}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{1}{2x+C}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-333805" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=x+7$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8{y}^{2}-16(x+7)y+8(x+7)^{2}+1\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8{y}^{2}-16(x+7)y+8(x+7)^{2}+1,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=8,\\,b(x)=-16(x+7),\\,c(x)=8(x+7)^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=x+7.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=1$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+x+7\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+1.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+1=8(z+x+7)^{2}-16(x+7)(z+x+7)+8(x+7)^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+1 & =8((x+7)^{2}+2(x+7)z+{z}^{2})-16(x+7)(z+x+7)+8(x+7)^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{′}+1 & =8{z}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =8{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =8{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =8x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{8x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-(x+7)$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{8x+C} \\\\ y-(x+7) & =-\\frac{1}{8x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{8x+C}+x+7 \\\\  & =x+7-\\frac{1}{8x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-334137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=x+7+\\frac{1}{8x+C}"] ["math" "y=x+7+\\frac{2}{8x+C}"] ["math" "y=x+7+\\frac{2}{8x-C}"] ["math" "y=x+7-\\frac{1}{8x+C}"] ["math" "y=x+7-\\frac{1}{x+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=x+7-\\frac{1}{8x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,y+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,y+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=2x,\\,b(x)=-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,c(x)=2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2x\\,(z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,(z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2x({z}^{2}+2z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,(z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2x{z}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-334122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-C}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=x+1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}-6(x+1)y+3{x}^{2}+6x+4\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}-6(x+1)y+3{x}^{2}+6x+4,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=3,\\,b(x)=-6(x+1),\\,c(x)=3{x}^{2}+6x+4.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=x+1.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=1$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+x+1\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+1.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+1=3(z+x+1)^{2}-6(x+1)(z+x+1)+3{x}^{2}+6x+4.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+1 & =3((x+1)^{2}+2(x+1)z+{z}^{2})-6(x+1)(z+x+1)+3{x}^{2}+6x+4 \\\\ {z}^{′}+1 & =3{z}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =3x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-(x+1)$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y-(x+1) & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}+x+1 \\\\  & =x+1-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13607c35145ece188db797b7266011b9a6c65d49515a6220e7593aef13bca439"} {"question" "q-334096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=x+1+\\frac{1}{3x+C}"] ["math" "y=x+1+\\frac{2}{3x+C}"] ["math" "y=x+1+\\frac{2}{3x-C}"] ["math" "y=x+1-\\frac{1}{3x+C}"] ["math" "y=x+1-\\frac{1}{x+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "q-334096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=x+1-\\frac{1}{3x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/state.json" "file_sha256" "0baa70b4ce6b0f3866d16dc51651425aab919b7f16261db88729dacde17072b8"} {"question" "e-21079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n- $y' = 4xy^2 - 3y + 1$\n\n- $y' - 2y = (x^2 + 5)y^2 + \\sin(x)$\n\n- $y' = e^xy^3 + y - x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/example-21079.json" "file_sha256" "428180110c199764fcc14299c6f1735c47aa4c2cd6338a16f9be3a6dcd922701"} {"question" "e-21079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x) = 4x, \\qquad b(x)=-3, \\qquad c(x)=1.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\ny' = (x^2 + 5)y^2 + \\sin(x) + 2y.\n$$\n\nThis is a Riccati differential equation with\n\n$$\na(x) = x^2 + 5, \\qquad b(x)=2, \\qquad c(x)=\\sin(x).\n$$\n\n- Equation III is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\ny' = e^xy^3 + y - x.\n$$\n\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a $y^3$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/example-21079.json" "file_sha256" "428180110c199764fcc14299c6f1735c47aa4c2cd6338a16f9be3a6dcd922701"} {"question" "e-21080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function $y_0(x) = 1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\ny' = 3y^2 - 7y + 4.\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^n\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/example-21080.json" "file_sha256" "c8f31922a8e9bd8cd2a7580545df571653f0b2036aba5a5af1967c5aaf2d4816"} {"question" "e-21080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x) = z(x) + y_0(x),\n$$\n\nwhere $y_0(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\ny'(x) = z'(x) + y_0'(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $y_0(x) = 1.$ Since $y_0'(x) = 0$, we have\n\n$$\ny = z + 1 \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad y' = z'.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\nz' = 3(z + 1)^2 - 7(z + 1) + 4.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′} & =3(z+1)^{2}-7(z+1)+4 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =3{z}^{2}-z \\\\ {z}^{′}+z & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{ \\textrm{d} z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^n\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x) = 1, \\qquad \nQ(x) = 3, \\qquad \nn = 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/example-21080.json" "file_sha256" "c8f31922a8e9bd8cd2a7580545df571653f0b2036aba5a5af1967c5aaf2d4816"} {"question" "e-21081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y_0(x) = 4x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\ny' = 2x\\,y^2 - 16x^2 y + 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/example-21081.json" "file_sha256" "3c0bf7cb186054519b31b045033ff37b7e3b58a481cf1ead1e29c12ee81c3d36"} {"question" "e-21081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\ny' = 2x\\,y^2 - 16x^2 y + 32x^3 + 4,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x) = 2x, \\qquad b(x) = -16x^2, \\qquad c(x) = 32x^3 + 4.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x) = z(x) + y_0(x),\n$$\n\nwhere $y_0(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\ny'(x) = z'(x) + y_0'(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $y_0(x) = 4x.$ Since $y_0'(x) = 4$, we have\n\n$$\ny = z + 4x \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad y' = z' + 4.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\nz' + 4 = 2x\\,(z + 4x)^2 - 16x^2 (z + 4x) + 32x^3 + 4.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+4 & =2x({z}^{2}+8xz+16{x}^{2})-16{x}^{2}(z+4x)+32{x}^{3}+4 \\\\ {z}^{′}+4 & =2x{z}^{2}+4 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z = y-4x$ to recover the initial variable $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y-4x & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}+4x \\\\  & =4x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054267/example-21081.json" "file_sha256" "3c0bf7cb186054519b31b045033ff37b7e3b58a481cf1ead1e29c12ee81c3d36"}] "usage" {"e-21079" [] "q-333306" [] "q-333607" [] "e-21081" [] "q-333805" [] "e-21080" []} "basis" 1794 "retractions" [[17592186217738 :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n1. $y^{′} = y^{3} - 2xy + 4$\n2. $y^{′} = 6xy^{2} + 3y - x$\n3. $y^{′} + 5y = 2x^{2}y^{2} + 7$"] [17592186217739 :question/problem "The function $y_{0}(x) = 1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n$y^{′} = y^{2} - 3y + 2$.\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n$\\frac{dz}{dx} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^{n}$\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$, and the value of $n$.$P(x) =$\n{{field-1}}\n$, Q(x) =$\n{{field-2}}\n$, n =$\n{{field-3}}"] [17592186217740 :question/problem "Given that $y_{0}(x) = \\frac{2}{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$y^{′} = y^{2} - \\frac{4}{x}y + \\frac{2}{x^{2}}$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation."] [17592186216937 :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Riccati differential equation?\n\n1. $y' = 4xy^2 - 3y + 1$\n2. $y' - 2y = (x^2 + 5)y^2 + \\sin(x)$\n3. $y' = e^xy^3 + y - x$"] [17592186216937 :question/worked-solution "A first-order differential equation is a Riccati differential equation if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Riccati differential equation with\n$a(x) = 4x, \\qquad b(x)=-3, \\qquad c(x)=1$.\n- Equation II is a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n$y' = (x^2 + 5)y^2 + \\sin(x) + 2y$.\nThis is a Riccati differential equation with\n$a(x) = x^2 + 5, \\qquad b(x)=2, \\qquad c(x)=\\sin(x)$.\n- Equation III is not a Riccati differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n$y' = e^xy^3 + y - x$.\nThis is not a Riccati differential equation since it includes a $y^3$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] [17592186216938 :question/problem "The function $y_0(x) = 1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n$y' = 3y^2 - 7y + 4$.\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^n$\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$, and the value of $n$."] [17592186216938 :question/worked-solution "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x)\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x) = z(x) + y_0(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $y_0(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\ny'(x) = z'(x) + y_0'(x)\n$$\n\nIn our case, $y_0(x) = 1$. Since $y_0'(x) = 0$, we have\n\n$$\ny = z + 1 \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad y' = z'\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\nz' = 3(z + 1)^2 - 7(z + 1) + 4\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz^{′} &= 3(z + 1)^{2} - 7(z + 1) + 4 \\\\\nz^{′} &= 3z^{2} - z \\\\\nz^{′} + z &= 3z^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d} z}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^n\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x) = 1, \\qquad Q(x) = 3, \\qquad n = 2\n$$"] [17592186216939 :question/problem "Given that $y_0(x) = 4x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$y' = 2x\\,y^2 - 16x^2 y + 32x^3 + 4$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation."] [17592186216939 :question/worked-solution "The equation\n\n$$\ny' = 2x\\,y^2 - 16x^2 y + 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\ny' = a(x)y^2 + b(x)y + c(x)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x) = 2x, \\qquad b(x) = -16x^2, \\qquad c(x) = 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x) = z(x) + y_0(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $y_0(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\ny'(x) = z'(x) + y_0'(x)\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\ny_0(x) = 4x\n$$\n\nSince $y_0'(x) = 4$, we have\n\n$$\ny = z + 4x \\qquad \\Rightarrow \\qquad y' = z' + 4\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\nz' + 4 = 2x\\,(z + 4x)^2 - 16x^2 (z + 4x) + 32x^3 + 4\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz^{′} + 4 &= 2x(z^{2} + 8xz + 16x^{2}) - 16x^{2}(z + 4x) + 32x^{3} + 4 \\\\\nz^{′} + 4 &= 2xz^{2} + 4 \\\\\nz^{′} &= 2xz^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dz}{dx} &= 2xz^{2} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{z^{2}}\\frac{dz}{dx} &= 2x \\\\\n∫\\frac{1}{z^{2}}\\frac{dz}{dx}dx &= ∫2xdx \\\\\n∫z^{-2}dz &= ∫2xdx \\\\\n- \\frac{1}{z} &= x^{2} + C \\\\\nz &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z = y-4x$ to recover the initial variable $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C} \\\\\ny - 4x &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{1}{x^{2} + C} + 4x \\\\\n&= 4x - \\frac{1}{x^{2} + C}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186216523 17592186216524 17592186216525 17592186216526 17592186216527 17592186216532 17592186216533 17592186216534 17592186216535 17592186216536] "immutable_fields" [[17592186216522 :answer-field/correct] [17592186216522 :answer-field/id] [17592186216522 :answer-field/key] [17592186216522 :answer-field/type] [17592186216528 :answer-field/id] [17592186216528 :answer-field/key] [17592186216528 :answer-field/type] [17592186216529 :answer-field/id] [17592186216529 :answer-field/key] [17592186216529 :answer-field/type] [17592186216530 :answer-field/id] [17592186216530 :answer-field/key] [17592186216530 :answer-field/type] [17592186216531 :answer-field/correct] [17592186216531 :answer-field/id] [17592186216531 :answer-field/key] [17592186216531 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
